    }

    for (int i = 0; i < num_batches; i++) {
        pthread_join(threads[i], NULL);
    }

    return 0;
}
```

This code snippet demonstrates a basic implementation of a function to process network packet batches in C. It includes dynamic memory allocation and deallocation, handling of payload size limits, and thread safety using POSIX threads (pthread). The `packet_processing_thread` function processes each packet batch concurrently, ensuring that no memory leaks occur and that the total memory usage remains within specified limits.']

